From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:54:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 247/638] base: launch AROS children with CreateNewProc
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model

AI_STATUS: hosted-validated, native-pending

ROOT_CAUSE: AROS base::LaunchProcess returned ENOSYS, preventing Chromium from creating independent child processes even though DOS/Exec already provides tracked child creation and posixc waitpid consumes NP_NotifyOnDeath state.

FIX_REASON: Load the native executable, quote AmigaDOS arguments, launch with CreateNewProc and NP_NotifyOnDeath, expose the ETask ID as Chromium process handle, and fail closed for unsupported POSIX-only launch options.

SCOPE: base/process/launch_aros.cc only. MessagePort/Mojo transport and child-role enablement remain separate phases.

VALIDATION: launch_aros.o and launch_process_aros_probe build. Clean hosted AROS observed parent 35, child 36, exact argv, three-second concurrent lifetime, child exit 23, and successful WaitForExit. Evidence: /home/terminills/Documents/GitHub/chromium-aros/test-artifacts/hosted-20260716-process-model. Native SMP validation delegated as.

RISK: moderate. fd remapping, environment replacement, pre-exec delegates, rlimits, and process groups remain fail-closed; native SMP result is pending.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap,,
